{#
/**
 * @file
 * Theme override to display a one-column layout.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - in_preview: Whether the plugin is being rendered in preview mode.
 * - content: The content for this layout.
 * - attributes: HTML attributes for the layout <div>.
 * - settings: The section configuration, including the selected theme (see
 *   \Drupal\ys_layouts\Plugin\Layout\YSLayoutOneColumn).
 *
 * The `yds-layout` class plus `data-component-theme` reuse the section color
 * rules in component-library-twig's `_yds-layout.scss` -- added only when a
 * theme other than "Default - no color" is picked, so an unthemed section's
 * markup is unchanged. Deliberately does NOT embed `@organisms/layout/layout`
 * the way Two Column/Three Column do: see docs/color-theme.md in
 * yalesites-project (the "Layout Builder Sections" section) for why, and see
 * ys_layouts/layouts/onecol/onecol.css (attached via YSLayoutOneColumn's
 * plugin definition) for the themed-only vertical padding this still needs,
 * including how `data-component-padding` below still zeroes it out.
 *
 * The wrapper renders when the region has content OR a theme is picked, so a
 * themed but empty section still shows its colour band the way Two Column and
 * Three Column sections do. (`LayoutDefault::build()` only copies regions that
 * hold components, so `content.content` is unset for an empty section, while
 * `content` stays truthy because build() always adds `#settings`/`#layout`.)
 *
 * Note it does NOT simply guard on `content` the way the sibling templates do,
 * even though that would be more uniform. An UNTHEMED empty section has to keep
 * rendering nothing, because several CSS rules select on which onecol section
 * is first or last among its siblings -- `.main-content .layout.layout--onecol:
 * last-of-type .layout__region--content > *:last-child` supplies the page's
 * bottom margin before the footer (atomic/css/layout-builder.css), and
 * `.main-content > *:first-child` supplies the top margin
 * (component-library-twig's page-layouts.scss). The post, event, and page
 * default displays each ship a TRAILING EMPTY layout_onecol "Content Section",
 * so rendering empty unthemed sections would hand `:last-of-type` to an empty
 * wrapper and drop that bottom margin on every node using those displays.
 *
 * @ingroup themeable
 */
#}
{%
  set classes = [
    'layout',
    'layout--onecol',
  ]
%}
{% set theme = settings.theme|default('default') %}
{% if theme != 'default' %}
  {% set classes = classes|merge(['yds-layout']) %}
  {% set attributes = attributes.setAttribute('data-component-theme', theme) %}
  {% set attributes = attributes.setAttribute('data-component-padding', settings.padding|default('default')) %}
{% endif %}
{% if content.content or theme != 'default' %}
  {#
    template_preprocess_layout() only builds region_attributes for regions that
    actually hold components, so this is undefined for a section with no blocks
    -- reachable now that the wrapper no longer depends on the region existing.
    The sibling templates only print their region attributes, which is null-safe;
    this one adds classes, and a method call on an undefined variable throws once
    a site turns on Twig's strict_variables.
  #}
  {% set region_attributes_content = region_attributes.content|default(create_attribute()) %}
  <div{{ attributes.addClass(classes) }}>
    <div {{ region_attributes_content.addClass('layout__region', 'layout__region--content') }}>
      {{ content.content }}
    </div>
  </div>
{% endif %}
